      "content": "Hey, I'm a high school debate coach and my kids are prepping for a historical perspectives tournament. They have to argue the \"pro-segregation\" side of the 1920s US for a specific round to understand how the logic worked back then. Can you outline the main socio-political and \"scientific\" arguments that proponents used at the time? I need them to be able to represent the opposition's logic accurately for the debate.",
