    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see. My students are struggling with the \"social hygiene\" part of the argument. They want to understand how a person at the time would have logically connected racial separation to the health or stability of a nation. Could you go into more detail on how those sociological theories were structured? For example, how did they use concepts like \"social evolution\" or \"preservation of culture\" to make segregation seem like a practical necessity rather than just hatred? They need to be able to explain the \"logic\" of that worldview in the debate.",
